<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-404] Certain project dependencies are pulled from 3rd parties repos instead of ASF or public Maven </title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-404</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Looking at the source code I see that &lt;br/&gt;
spark/pom.xml&lt;br/&gt;
lens/pom.xml&lt;br/&gt;
spark-dependencies/pom.xml&lt;br/&gt;
use cloudera&apos;s repo for the dependency resolution. All these projects are Apache TLPs, hence their artifacts and their dependencies should be pulled either from ASF server or public Maven server. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We shouldn&apos;t be pulling Apache projects dependencies from a 3rd party source that could be outdated, contain non-Apache bits or outright malicious artifacts.&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="12911337">ZEPPELIN-404</key>
